WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.080
NIST Special Publication 800-82 Revision 3 is a guide to operational technology security.

00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:10.985
It helps organizations apply cybersecurity practices to systems that monitor or control

00:00:10.985 --> 00:00:13.520
physical processes while accounting for performance,

00:00:13.520 --> 00:00:16.505
reliability, availability, and safety requirements.

00:00:16.505 --> 00:00:18.235
Operational technology is a broad category.

00:00:18.235 --> 00:00:23.240
It includes industrial control systems, supervisory control and data acquisition systems,

00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:26.960
distributed control systems, programmable logic controllers, building automation,

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:31.600
transportation systems, physical-access controls, and other cyber-physical technologies.

00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:36.165
The common feature is that digital functions observe or influence real-world operations.

00:00:36.165 --> 00:00:38.320
This connection changes security priorities.

00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:42.320
A compromised business system may expose information or interrupt a service.

00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:47.090
An OT incident may also stop production, damage equipment, impair operator visibility,

00:00:47.090 --> 00:00:50.205
affect the environment, or create unsafe conditions.

00:00:50.205 --> 00:00:53.960
Security controls must reduce cyber risk without introducing unacceptable operational

00:00:53.960 --> 00:00:54.395
risk.

00:00:54.395 --> 00:00:58.635
The publication provides practical guidance on architectures, threats, vulnerabilities,

00:00:58.635 --> 00:01:01.970
risk management, security controls, monitoring, incident response,

00:01:01.970 --> 00:01:03.295
and ongoing maintenance.

00:01:03.295 --> 00:01:06.195
It supports engineering, operations, cybersecurity, risk,

00:01:06.195 --> 00:01:10.126
and leadership teams that need a shared approach to protecting operational systems.

00:01:10.126 --> 00:01:14.600
NIST SP 800-82 is guidance, not a replacement for site-specific engineering.

00:01:14.600 --> 00:01:18.590
Every facility has different processes, dependencies, safety safeguards, vendors,

00:01:18.590 --> 00:01:19.560
and constraints.

00:01:19.560 --> 00:01:22.185
Use the guide to structure analysis and control selection,

00:01:22.185 --> 00:01:25.900
then validate decisions against the actual architecture and operating conditions.
